        },
        {
            "👥",
            "A team planned for one mode stays there",
            "A team the planner put aside for a dungeon room only goes on in that dungeon, and a team put aside more than 30 minutes ago is dropped. Before, last night's dungeon team went on at the start of an Infinite run.",
            "FIXED"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.8",
    date = "Nov 17, 2026",
    title = "Faster planning and placing",
    items = {
        {
            "⚡",
            "Faster spot search and road maths",
            "The road is kept as segments in a grid: where an enemy is on the road is worked out exactly (no more steps between samples), and the spot search and road cover only look at the road near a spot. The facing of line and cone attacks is aimed at where enemies really are.",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "🧮",
            "Faster simulator",
            "The enemy-HP limit of a team is found by halving instead of trying every step (about 4 runs instead of up to 11), and the simulator's income window costs the same at any length. Zero costs can no longer divide by zero in the upgrade maths.",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "🎯",
            "Abilities don't wait for each other",
            "One unit's ability request no longer holds back every other unit. The infinite buff still casts one copy at a time, so its order stays right.",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "🧹",
            "Unused code removed",
            "Old comparison and relay-buff helpers that nothing called any more.",
            "IMPROVED"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.7",
    date = "Nov 17, 2026",
    title = "Infinite buff fixed, buff test",
    items = {
        {
            "🥁",
            "The infinite buff waits for 4 copies",
            "Commander, Windsong and Leafy no longer cast with one to three copies down: the rotation starts only when 4 copies stand within each other's range (each one reaches every other), so every cast lands on a copy that is already buffed. Before, the first copies cast early and their cooldowns ran out of step, so the buff never reached +100%.",
            "FIXED"
        },
        {
            "⛓️",
            "It doesn't stop between waves",
            "Once the rotation runs it keeps going with no enemies on the field and with no attacker in range. A pause there used to break the chain.",
            "FIXED"
        },
        {
            "📍",
            "Copies placed as one group",
            "The next copy now has to reach every copy already down, and spots around the group are tried too. Before, a copy could land out of range when no attacker stood nearby.",
            "FIXED"
        },
        {
            "🧪",
            "Battle → Testing: infinite buff test",
            "Turn the test on and start a match: once 4 copies stand within each other's range the rotation starts even with no enemies, and the page shows each cast, the buff level the game reports, how long +100% holds, whether the cooldown fits the loop, and a verdict: WORKS, PARTLY or NOT WORKING with the reason. The last result stays there after the match.",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.6",
    date = "Nov 16, 2026",
    title = "Farming: Quick Start and Routines",
    items = {
        {
            "🚀",
            "Quick Start",
            "Farming → Quick Start: pick a Mode, a Map (and a Difficulty for story acts), set Runs, press Start Farming. The last setup comes back next time. Optional settings (Auto Buff, buff type, matchmaking, ending Infinite early) sit under Advanced Settings, and a missing field is named before anything starts.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "📋",
            "Routines",
            "Farming → Routines: save named queues of tasks, each with its own map, difficulty and settings. Add, edit, reorder and delete tasks. Start Routine plays each task until its runs are done, then switches to the next one by itself, and stops after the last.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "📊",
            "Progress, Stop and Retry",
            "Task 1 of 3 · Story → Planet Namak (Hard) · 12/50. A run counts once, when the game confirms the win (Infinite: when it ends); a loss, a failed start or a disconnect counts nothing. Stop lets the current match finish and starts nothing after it. A start that keeps failing pauses the farm with the reason, and Retry goes on from the confirmed count. Only one farm runs at a time.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🛡️",
            "Your Auto Farm settings stay yours",
            "Quick Start and Routines lay their settings over Auto Farm only while they run. Your own settings are what gets saved, what the Stages, Challenges, Events, Party and Rules pages show, and what comes back when the farm ends.",
            "IMPROVED"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.5",
    date = "Nov 16, 2026",
    title = "Performance tab",
    items = {
        {
            "⚡",
            "Its own tab",
            "Textures, effects, lighting, 3D and the FPS cap now sit in their own Performance tab in the side menu. In 2.4 that section was not registered in the window's layout, so the window stopped building there and the section never showed.",
            "FIXED"
        },
        {
            "🔁",
            "A new version takes over",
            "Starting a newer file while an older copy runs used to do nothing, so the old window stayed. Now the old copy saves and closes, and the new version opens.",
            "FIXED"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.4",
    date = "Nov 16, 2026",
    title = "Lighter graphics",
    items = {
        {
            "🖼️",
            "Hide or delete textures",
            "Settings → Performance: decals, surface textures and mesh skins on the map can be hidden (undo any time) or deleted (frees memory; they come back on the next map or after a rejoin). Units and characters keep their look. Parts, the road and the map folders are never touched, so placement keeps working.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "✨",
            "Hide or delete effects",
            "Particles, trails, beams, smoke, fire and lights, attack effects included. Effects that appear during a match are hidden at once and deleted a few seconds later, when the game is done with them.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "💡",
            "Simple lighting, 3D off, FPS cap",
            "No shadows, bloom, blur, fog or water waves and the lowest render quality; a switch that stops drawing the world (the farm keeps playing); and an FPS cap when your executor has setfpscap. Everything here is undone when you turn it off.",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.3",
    date = "Nov 16, 2026",
    title = "Auto Buff",
    items = {
        {
            "🥁",
            "Buff rotation",
            "Commander (physical), Windsong and Leafy (magic) copies cast in turn so each buff lands on an already buffed buffer and the bonus climbs in steps. With four copies: #1, #2 four seconds later (five for Windsong and Leafy), #3 when #1's buff drops, #4 when #2's drops. With one to three copies the partial buff is kept for a boss or pressure. A failed cast or a sold copy is worked around.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "📍",
            "Buffers stand as a group",
            "The next copy goes where it reaches the copies already down and they reach it, with the matching attackers inside. When the group does not fit, the real coverage is used.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🧮",
            "Counted before and during a match",
            "The team search and every buy use the rotation's average bonus, not a guess: a new buffer copy, a buffer upgrade that widens its circle, a new attacker and an attacker upgrade are compared by what they add to the whole team.",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "🎛️",
            "Switch, type and status",
            "Battle → Controls: Auto Buff on or off, Auto / Physical / Magic, and a status line with the copies down, the effect and why it waits. A bonus is shown as seen only when the game reports it; otherwise it is marked as an estimate.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🧹",
            "TESTING tab removed",
            "The test page is gone from the window.",
            "IMPROVED"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.10",
    date = "Nov 17, 2026",
    title = "Auto Buff: squad template, relay copies and cooldown check",
    items = {
        {
            "⏱️",
            "Pre-match cooldown check",
            "In the lobby, Auto Buff checks your Commander, Windsong or Leafy cooldown against 2 × buff duration (reading the unit's curse when visible, or the real cooldown measured in your last match) and shows whether Lenio's order fits or needs an SPA curse.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "📐",
            "4-copy squad placed as a template",
            "When the first copy is bought, 4 mutually linked spots near your attackers and the road are chosen at once, and the next copies go straight into that template (recalculated if a spot is taken or refused).",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "📡",
            "5th and 6th relay copies",
            "Once the 4-copy rotation is running, up to 2 extra relay copies can be bought when they beat the next damage upgrade. They stand on the edge of the squad's range to reach distant attackers and cast at +100% without touching the 4-copy Lenio rotation.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🎯",
            "Attackers prioritize the 4-copy buff zone",
            "Attackers whose damage type matches the buffer choose a spot covered by all 4 squad copies whenever it reaches at least 60% of the road samples of the best unbuffed spot.",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "🧪",
            "Richer buff test and cast failure reasons",
            "Failed casts now log what the game answered and which copy tried to cast. Battle → Testing shows the squad template, cooldown check, relay copies and how much attacker damage stands under the full squad, relay copies or outside the buff.",
            "IMPROVED"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.11",
    date = "Nov 17, 2026",
    title = "Dungeon: path planning",
    items = {
        {
            "🧭",
            "Dungeon path planner",
            "Before each dungeon room, every path through the rooms the game shows (the rooms on offer and the rooms each one opens next) is scored in expected gems: chests count only if the run reaches room 20, so the chests you hold ride on every risky room; a curse lowers the win chance of the rooms after it (in the simulator); each lost try costs one Dungeon Room Value. Rooms past what the game shows are estimated from the rooms seen at that depth.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "📜",
            "The log shows the paths",
            "The log lists each path with its win chances, curses, chance to reach room 20 and expected gems, then the chosen path and what puts it ahead. The dungeon box in Raids and Dungeon shows the plan.",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.12",
    date = "Nov 18, 2026",
    title = "Discord and Auto Rejoin",
    items = {
        {
            "📨",
            "Discord messages",
            "Paste your own Discord webhook in Settings → Discord and reconnect: a message after every match (result, wave, time, gems, coins, items and the session so far), a session summary every few hours, and alerts when the farm stops, makes no progress or loses the connection. The link stays in settings.json on your PC and the window never shows its key.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🔌",
            "Auto Rejoin",
            "After a lost connection, a timeout or a server shutdown the farm joins the lobby again, starts itself there and goes on. Never after a kick, a ban or a login from another device, and at most 3 tries in 15 minutes.",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.13",
    date = "Nov 18, 2026",
    title = "Richer reports",
    items = {
        {
            "🌀",
            "More in the match message",
            "The Discord message after a match now says what it was: a portal's tier, modifiers and how many like it are left; the challenge; the element buffs (what enemies take more from, what they resist); for a dungeon the room, tries left, chests, curses and the planned path. The script version is at the bottom.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "📋",
            "Compact results",
            "Settings → Discord and reconnect → Compact Results: one line per match, several matches in one short list.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "⚙️",
            "Performance report",
            "Performance tab: FPS, memory, ping and the script's own memory now, plus the session's average and worst FPS and how much memory grew. The Discord summary carries the same.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🔁",
            "Team change log",
            "Every team swap the farm makes is written to team-changes.log in the script's folder: who went out, who came in, why, and whether the game took it.",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.14",
    date = "Nov 18, 2026",
    title = "Smarter upgrades, faster placement plan",
    items = {
        {
            "📐",
            "Range upgrades count",
            "An upgrade that widens a unit's circle is now valued by how much more road the unit reaches from where it stands. Before, an upgrade that only added range was worth nothing to Smart Autoplay, and range on top of damage was undervalued.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🪜",
            "Weak step before a strong one",
            "When the next upgrade adds little but the one after hits more enemies at once, the pair is judged on equal terms, area of effect included.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🌾",
            "Safer farms with random units",
            "With random equipped units a cheap farm is only bought when the defense still keeps up with the next waves after paying for it.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "⚡",
            "Faster placement plan",
            "The placement plan no longer simulates the same layout twice, and the team search keeps to its time budget.",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.15",
    date = "Nov 18, 2026",
    title = "Range judged on the real road in the planner",
    items = {
        {
            "🗺️",
            "Planner sees the road",
            "When the planner's simulation weighs a range upgrade, it now counts the stretch of road the wider circle adds from the unit's planned spot, the same road it deals damage on. A range upgrade that reaches no new road is no longer bought in the simulation, and one that reaches a bend is valued for it.",
            "FIX"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.16",
    date = "Nov 18, 2026",
    title = "More runs per hour, fairer spot memory",
    items = {
        {
            "⏱️",
            "Faster team when it is safe",
            "When two lineups both clear a mode with room to spare (they still win against enemies with 30% more HP), the planner now takes the one that finishes sooner: more runs, so more rewards, per hour. The short-mode farm rule and endless modes are not affected.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🧠",
            "Spot memory that forgets",
            "Wins and losses at a spot used to add up forever, and one loss weighed as much as seven wins. Now older runs fade, a loss is mostly blamed on the whole placement plan rather than on every spot in it, and all this history together moves a plan by about one wave at most: enough to steer away from a plan that keeps losing, not enough to overrule the simulator.",
            "FIX"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.17",
    date = "Nov 18, 2026",
    title = "Buffer pairs in the team search",
    items = {
        {
            "🤝",
            "Buffer with the right partner",
            "When the team search tries bringing in a buffer, it now brings it with the strongest free attacker of the damage type that buffer raises (up to two buffers are tried), instead of whichever attacker came first.",
            "FIX"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.18",
    date = "Nov 18, 2026",
    title = "Tier list of your units",
    items = {
        {
            "🏆",
            "Tier list from your own units",
            "Each plan now spends part of its time measuring your units in the simulator: how much each one adds to your team on this mode. They are ranked S / A / B / C per mode and remembered. The best go first in the team search, so a strong cheap unit the old formula overlooked is no longer missed, and with a big collection the weakest stop taking the search's time. Shown in Battle → Planner → Plan (Tier list) and in the log.",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.19",
    date = "Nov 18, 2026",
    title = "Fused Hero in the tier list, safer plans",
    items = {
        {
            "🐉",
            "Fused Hero in the tier list",
            "Carrot and Vego are measured together, with the fusion, and shown as one line: Fused Hero (Carrot + Vego). When it ranks S or A, both go first in the team search. Units with passives the simulator does not model are marked * until 3 real runs with them have corrected their damage.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🛡️",
            "Room to spare, three ways",
            "A faster lineup now counts as safe only if it also wins when its real damage is 15% under the estimate and when enemies walk 15% faster, not only against thicker enemies.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🕊️",
            "Flying enemies checked apart",
            "Before a farm buy, Smart Autoplay checks coming flying enemies against the damage of the units that can hit the air, not against the whole team's damage.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🗺️",
            "Calibration per map",
            "A new mode on a map you already farm starts from what real runs on that map taught, not from the average of all maps.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🔁",
            "Units trade places",
            "The placement plan also tries two units swapping spots, a move no single unit can make when every good spot is taken.",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.20",
    date = "Nov 18, 2026",
    title = "Spots that suit the attack's shape",
    items = {
        {
            "📐",
            "Placement knows the attack's shape",
            "A line attack is worth more where the road runs straight along its hit, a circle where the road folds and enemies bunch, a cone where road lies in front of the unit. The placement plan now measures this for every spot a unit can stand on, adds the spots that suit its shape to the ones it tries, and its simulation gives each spot its own number of enemies per hit. The log shows it per unit (for example \"circle attack: ×1.40 of an ordinary spot's extra targets\").",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🎯",
            "One hit, the right number of targets",
            "The simulator let a hit reach one enemy too many: that enemy took no damage but still got the stun or slow, bleed and shield chip. A single-target stunner counted as stunning two. Fixed, so control units are no longer overrated.",
            "FIX"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.21",
    date = "Nov 18, 2026",
    title = "Fairer learning, smarter Infinite exits",
    items = {
        {
            "📈",
            "Fair unit learning",
            "What a unit could deal is now summed second by second while it stood and had a target. A unit placed or upgraded late is no longer marked weaker than it is, in the simulator and in the tier list.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "✨",
            "One rule for abilities",
            "The simulator now fires abilities by the same rule as the match: at once for a boss or an enemy near the base, and not on an almost dead group.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "⏳",
            "Whole run cycle per mode",
            "Mode choice counts how long wins and losses take and what a loss pays, and a new mode's bonus for a try fades over ten runs instead of stopping after two.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🎯",
            "Calibration per measure",
            "Enemy speed, damage, yen and the rest each count their own observations: the first real damage reading counts in full.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "♾️",
            "Infinite: is the rest worth it?",
            "After the daily gems, the run goes on while the next waves (up to ten ahead, from your past runs on this mode) pay more per minute than the best other mode.",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.22",
    date = "Nov 18, 2026",
    title = "Attack shape everywhere, a look ahead before farms",
    items = {
        {
            "📐",
            "One line shape",
            "A line attack is measured the same way when the script scores a spot and when it turns the unit: by the attack's own width when the game gives one.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🧭",
            "Attack shape off the plan",
            "When a unit has no planned spot (or it is taken), and in the kill box, fast style and for units that stun or slow, the best spots by road are re-ranked by the unit's attack shape, as the placement plan does.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🔮",
            "A look ahead before a farm",
            "When enemies already get some way down the road and the economy wants a farm, the simulator plays the next 5 waves from this very moment, with the farm and with more damage. If the farm costs the base, damage goes first.",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.23",
    date = "Nov 18, 2026",
    title = "Smarter farm buying",
    items = {
        {
            "💴",
            "Best farm order",
            "Which farm to buy next is found by playing the next buys forward wave by wave: buy the farm you can afford now or save for a better one, three small upgrades or one big one. The order that ends the match with the most yen goes first.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "♾️",
            "Farms in Infinite",
            "In Infinite a farm must pay back within the waves your past runs on this mode usually go on from here, not within a fixed look-ahead.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "⚖️",
            "Same team, same buys",
            "The number of attackers on the field is counted before the buy choice, so units early in the team no longer get a bonus the last ones don't, in the match and in the simulator.",
            "FIX"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.24",
    date = "Nov 19, 2026",
    title = "Buffers that reach your damage",
    items = {
        {
            "🎯",
            "Attackers step under the buff",
            "In a fast clear and in the kill zone, units a buffer raises now count the buff at a spot, as the other placements already did: they stand under all the rotation's copies when the road there is not much worse, instead of next to the squad.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "📍",
            "The squad stands by your real damage",
            "Where the 4 buffer copies go is weighed by the damage each unit really deals in the match, its summons' included, so a summoner is no longer read as weak. A unit's spot in the placement plan counts as much as its copies on the field.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🔁",
            "Relay copies priced by what they do",
            "A 5th or 6th relay copy is bought by how often relay copies really cast (here and in past matches), not by a guess. At the match's end a BUFF line shows how much damage stood under the whole squad, under relay copies and outside the buff, and who stood outside.",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.25",
    date = "Nov 19, 2026",
    title = "Your list of fixes",
    items = {
        {
            "🏠",
            "A simple Home",
            "Home now has everything to start: mode, map, difficulty, runs, Start and Stop, the 8 main switches and one line on what the farm is doing. Show advanced settings (on by default) hides or shows the other tabs; a search or a shortcut to one shows them again.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🃏",
            "Your own card list for the Summer Hunt",
            "Next to Card Pick: Take First (in order) and Never Take, card titles separated by commas. Attack takes every Attack tier, Attack II only that one. A card that would leave your team too weak is still skipped; Never Take wins over everything, and only when every offered card is banned does Card Pick choose.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🏰",
            "Dungeon paths with a forecast",
            "The dungeon plan now reads every layer the game shows (also when it lists the next rooms under a room), carries curses into the rooms after them and keeps coins back when two shops come in a row. The plan line says which path, its chance to finish the dungeon, the chest gems it expects and why not the best other first room. If a layer is hidden, it says so and picks room by room as before.",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "🚀",
            "More ways to lighten the game",
            "Performance → Lighting, 3D and FPS: Low Graphics Preset, Batch And Hide Effects (new effects too, in small batches), Pause 3D Outside Focus and Low CPU Panels. All of them undo themselves when switched off and never delete anything from the map.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🌾",
            "Farms out of the way",
            "Farms now look for spots up to 60 studs from the road (they stopped at 20) and take the one farthest from every road and off the planner's attacker spots, so the good spots stay free for damage. Battle → Farms Away From Road.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "👥",
            "With other players: hold the start",
            "When another player is in the match, your attackers stand nearer the start of the road and leave the end to them. Alone, or with an enemy leaking, placement works as before. Battle → With Other Players: Hold The Start.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🪜",
            "Buy order",
            "Battle → Buy Order: Smart (as before), Farms first or Team first. Farms first maxes the farms, then puts every unit of the team down, then works towards Fused Hero, then plays as usual. The order only holds while the defense does: with enemies near the base the farm buys damage first.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "💪",
            "Upgrades go to the units that really hit",
            "An upgrade is now weighed by the damage the unit really deals in the match (its summons' included), so a strong unit is upgraded before a weak one. After 40 s of saving with yen in hand, a useful buy that costs at most a third of it goes through (Spend Idle Yen).",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "♾️",
            "The infinite buff keeps its pace",
            "Without the SPA curse (cooldown over twice the buff, like the 64-65 s seen in your matches) the copies now cast one every quarter of the cooldown, 14 s of overlap to spare instead of 4, and a copy steps in early when the last buff is about to end. With the curse Lenio's order is unchanged.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🧬",
            "Fusion presses both",
            "If no Fused Hero appears 0.7 s after the first parent's press, the partner's Fusion is pressed too.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🤖",
            "The game's own Auto for buffers",
            "Press Auto on any unit's ability once: the farm learns the game's Auto command. When a buff rotation is steady at its top, the squad is switched to the game's Auto and the farm stops pressing it; if the buff drops, the farm takes the rotation back. Battle → Use Game Auto.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "⏱️",
            "Time left",
            "The match card shows the waves left as time (from the real length of the last waves), and the Record card shows gems per hour this session.",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.26",
    date = "Nov 19, 2026",
    title = "Your own team, and Fused Hero levels up",
    items = {
        {
            "👥",
            "Your own team for a mode",
            "Home: equip the six you want, then Save Equipped Team For This Mode. Before a run of that mode the farm puts that team on (even with Auto-Equip Best Team off), never swaps a unit out, and the simulator plans farms, buffs, Fusion and spots for it. Clear Team For This Mode gives the choice back to the farm.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🧬",
            "Fused Hero levels up",
            "Fused Hero's levels 2 and 3 hit slower than level 1, and the farm only looked two levels ahead, so it saw no gain and left the hero, often most of your damage, at level 1. It now weighs the whole road to level 6 (about +40% for the hero), as long as the yen still to come in the match pays for it.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "📊",
            "Levels at the end of a match",
            "A LEVELS line after the damage line: the highest level each unit reached on the field, Fused Hero first.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🃏",
            "Clearer card message",
            "When every offered card would take the team under its floor and nothing is on Never Take, the log says so instead of mentioning Never Take.",
            "IMPROVED"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.27",
    date = "Nov 19, 2026",
    title = "Choose what Auto Farm does",
    items = {
        {
            "🧭",
            "What Auto Farm does, on Home",
            "Under Main switches: tick the modes Smart may play (it picks whichever pays best of them) and the jobs it does between runs, such as making your team stronger, evolving, summoning or redeeming codes. The same settings as on the other tabs, so both always agree. Tick Every Mode puts every mode back and turns off every Only this; Just Play unticks every job. A line below says what it will do now.",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.28",
    date = "Nov 19, 2026",
    title = "A simpler window",
    items = {
        {
            "🏠",
            "Home: one Auto Farm block",
            "Tick the modes to play and the jobs between runs, then press Start Auto Farming (press it again to stop). It picks a team by itself; Pick Best Team does that now and equips it. Run setup, Farm control, the Interface switch and the Go to buttons are gone, and every tab is always shown. Go To Lobby and Start Farming Again are in Settings → General.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🗺️",
            "Farming: Modes and Queue",
            "Modes holds every mode on one page: a Play switch, its map and its settings, the Challenges, and Your Team For A Mode. Only this is gone (cleared once). Queue replaces Quick Start and Routines: add mode, map and runs, then Start Queue.",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "⏸️",
            "Smart Play For Units",
            "Units → Goals: one switch that pauses every Units job (upgrades, evolving, goals, training, limit breaks, summons) without touching their own switches, and turns them back on as they were.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🧪",
            "Battle → Testing removed",
            "The infinite buff test page is gone, and the test is off.",
            "IMPROVED"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.29",
    date = "Nov 19, 2026",
    title = "Dungeon farms, safer paths, units move up",
    items = {
        {
            "🌾",
            "Farms in the dungeon",
            "Summoners like Elyssia and units whose attack reaches flyers from some level now count as hitting the air in a match. Before, the farm thought nobody could kill the flyers coming, held every yen for damage, and placed farms late or never and didn't level them. Also, once flyers have been on the field for 30 s and none got past half the road, that forecast no longer holds farms back.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🗺️",
            "Safer dungeon paths",
            "A curse the simulator can't play now lowers the win chance of the rooms after it. A path with a new curse is taken only if it costs at most 5% win chance against the safest path without one (2% once curses would outnumber your buffs). An easier path within 150 gems of the best one is preferred.",
            "IMPROVED"
        },
        {
            "🔁",
            "Units move up at the end",
            "On the last wave, once no more enemies come, a unit every enemy left has walked past is sold and its yen goes to a spot ahead of them (Battle → Controls → Move Units At The End).",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.30",
    date = "Nov 20, 2026",
    title = "Back to the lobby even when a teleport fails",
    items = {
        {
            "🚪",
            "No more sitting in a finished match",
            "After a match the farm asked the game for the lobby only once. If that teleport failed, it stayed in the finished match until you came back. Now it watches the request: asks again every 20 s (sooner when the game reports a failed teleport), and after 6 tries teleports straight to the lobby the way Auto Rejoin does. Found by running the script for hours in a test sandbox with failing teleports.",
            "FIX"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.31",
    date = "Nov 20, 2026",
    title = "No more waiting forever on a lobby pad",
    items = {
        {
            "🪑",
            "A join without an answer is cleaned up",
            "When the game didn't answer a pad join in time but seated you anyway, the farm saw 'already in a lobby' and started no matches for hours. Now, after a join without an answer, it leaves that pad and checks again after 10, 35 and 80 s in case a late answer seated it. Only the pad the farm tried itself: a lobby you join by hand is never touched. Found by the test sandbox with slow server answers.",
            "FIX"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.32",
    date = "Nov 20, 2026",
    title = "No selling your defense to a boss that dies anyway",
    items = {
        {
            "🛡️",
            "Units behind the boss stay when the boss can't win",
            "In a boss fight the farm sold every unit the boss had walked past, every 2 s, even when the boss was going to die before the base. In long runs it then bought the same units back on the same spots a minute later and lost the upgrades. Now those units are sold only when the boss would really reach the base; otherwise they stay for the ordinary enemies that follow. Found by the test sandbox.",
            "FIX"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.33",
    date = "Nov 20, 2026",
    title = "Steadier team swaps, no buying after the end, no boss sell loop",
    items = {
        {
            "🔁",
            "Team swap waits for a free slot",
            "When taking a unit out got no answer and all 6 slots were still taken, the farm kept asking the game to put the new unit in, and the game kept refusing. Now it skips that and asks for the unit to go out again on the next round.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🏁",
            "Nothing is bought after the match ends",
            "If the match ended while a request was waiting for the game's answer, the farm could still try an upgrade right after. Now it checks the end of the match right before buying or upgrading.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "👑",
            "No sell-and-buy-back loop in a boss fight",
            "A unit sold because the boss had walked past it could be placed again on the very same spot a second later and sold again. Now that spot stays closed until the boss fight is over. Found by the test sandbox.",
            "FIX"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.34",
    date = "Nov 20, 2026",
    title = "Boss fights and dungeon chests",
    items = {
        {
            "👑",
            "New units go ahead of the boss",
            "After selling units the boss had walked past, the farm could put a new one on a spot right next to the old one, still behind the boss, and sell it again. Now, while that boss is on the field, a fighter is placed only where it reaches the road ahead of the boss.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🎁",
            "One lost answer no longer pauses the dungeon for 30 min",
            "If the game didn't answer one chest opening, the farm's own short request pause made the next tries look failed too, and the dungeon waited 30 minutes with the chests unopened. Now that pause is waited out, a real failure gets a few seconds before the next try, and if chests still don't open the farm comes back in 5 minutes.",
            "FIX"
        },
        {
            "🧠",
            "Replays no longer pile up in memory",
            "Each in-place replay starts the script again. Every new copy wrapped the game's server calls on top of the previous copy's wrapper, so all old copies stayed in memory and every call passed through all of them. After dozens of replays that was hundreds of MB and slower calls. Now each copy wraps the game's own functions, and old copies are released. Found by the test sandbox's memory check.",
            "FIX"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.35",
    date = "Nov 21, 2026",
    title = "Neural AI placement and targeting",
    items = {
        {
            "🧠",
            "Neural AI Placement (PlacementNN)",
            "Embedded a lightweight 36->64->32->1 neural network trained on 2D multi-lane combat simulations to pick optimal unit spots, 4-copy buff hubs, AoE line/cone/circle alignment, and far farm positions while keeping all emergency guardrails intact.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "🎯",
            "Neural AI Targeting (TargetNN)",
            "Embedded a 24->48->24->4 neural network that selects per-copy First, Last, Strongest, or Closest targeting based on AoE geometry, boss pressure, and split-targeting across copies (flyer and base-defense overrides always take priority).",
            "NEW"
        }
    }
})
table.insert(CHANGELOG, 1, {
    v = "2.36",
    date = "Nov 21, 2026",
    title = "Neural AI Smart Economy and Breakpoints",
    items = {
        {
            "💰",
            "Neural AI Economy (EconomyNN)",
            "Embedded a 28->48->24->1 neural network with 4-step breakpoint lookahead (Full AoE, Anti-Air, Bleed, CC, and 4-copy buffer cliques) to choose optimal build order, farming curves, and saving vs buying while preserving all emergency guardrails.",
            "NEW"
        },
        {
            "♻️",
            "Safe Midgame Starter Selling",
